// R11 gap 3 (docs/OWNERSHIP.md, "Still broken" table, row 3): an `arc` value
// unboxed for a `shared` parameter without ever being bound
// (`inspect(shared fresh())`) drops its handle on the floor. `fresh()`
// returns an already-retained `arc String` (R11 release rule 3); passed
// straight into `inspect`'s `shared String` parameter, `emitArcConversion`'s
// UNBOX case (have.shape == .arc, want.shape != .arc) reads the pointee
// through the handle and discards the handle itself, because the unbox exists
// to express the ONE deliberate non-retain (an `arc` PLACE passed to
// `shared`, safe by R8) and cannot tell that case apart from a temporary that
// was never a place at all and has no scope to release it in.
//
// `inspect` is declared bodyless on purpose, exactly as
// docs/OWNERSHIP.md and examples/arc.cell already do: only a real C
// definition can be measured against the `shared` calling convention at the
// boundary. examples/arc_host.c already defines `cell_inspect` with this
// exact signature (reads the borrowed view's length, retains and frees
// nothing), so this fixture is compiled against that file rather than a new
// one; tools/check.sh's `run_c_leaks` passes it the same way `run_c_host`
// already passes it for examples/arc.cell.
//
// This fixture ISOLATES that gap alone: `fresh()` boxes a literal into a
// fresh local (`let arc a = ...`) declared directly in `fresh`'s own body,
// not inside a block nested under a loop, so the block-scoped-local gap
// (examples/leaks/block_scoped_local.cell) cannot also fire here.
//
// Status: parses, passes `cell check`. LLVM and MLIR refuse it (arc is
// scalar-first-refused there, same as examples/arc.cell); lives under
// examples/leaks/ so it is invisible to the top-level examples/*.cell
// corpus, agreement, and mlir-lowering loops (see examples/leaks/README.md).

pub fn print_int(copy value: Int);

pub fn inspect(shared name: String) -> Int;

pub fn fresh() -> arc String {
    let arc a = "fresh"
    return a
}

pub fn main() {
    var i = 0
    var total = 0
    while i < 1000 {
        total = total + inspect(shared fresh())
        i = i + 1
    }
    print_int(total)
}
